---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Install guide — userscripts" description="Install ScriptCat, then install any script in this collection in three steps.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Install guide</p>
      <h1>Install a userscript in three steps</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        ScriptCat is the recommended manager: it installs from a raw URL, updates from GitHub, and
        keeps each script's settings in one panel. The steps below work the same way for every script
        in this collection.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>1. Install ScriptCat</h2>
      <p class="section__sub">Use the current stable release, which is the MV3 build.</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          Open <a href="https://scriptcat.org/">scriptcat.org</a> and choose your browser, or install
          "ScriptCat" from the Chrome Web Store, Microsoft Edge Add-ons, or Firefox Add-ons.
        </li>
        <li>
          Confirm the browser's permission prompt. ScriptCat asks for access to the sites you install
          scripts for; it does not need broad host access up front.
        </li>
        <li>
          Pin the ScriptCat icon to the toolbar so the script menu is one click away. Keep automatic
          updates switched on.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="install-note">
        Tampermonkey and Violentmonkey also run these scripts. ScriptCat is preferred because its
        install screen shows the full metadata, its update checks are reliable against
        <code>raw.githubusercontent.com</code>, and its per-script menu is where <strong>Settings…</strong>
        lives.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>2. Install the script</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>Open the script's page in this collection and press <strong>Add to ScriptCat</strong>.</li>
        <li>ScriptCat opens an install tab showing the name, version, matches, and grants. Read them, then press <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
        <li>Open the site the script targets. If the script adds a button or a key, it is active immediately — no reload needed unless the page says otherwise.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>3. Configure and update</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          Click the ScriptCat toolbar icon and choose the script's <strong>Settings…</strong>. Every
          option is in that one panel.
        </li>
        <li>
          Changes save as you make them and apply on the next page load. No option requires editing
          code.
        </li>
        <li>
          Updates arrive automatically from the repository's <code>main</code> branch. To force a
          check, open ScriptCat's script list and press <strong>Update</strong>.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li><strong>Nothing happens.</strong> Check that the script is enabled in ScriptCat and that the page URL matches the script's <code>@match</code> rules. Then reload the page.</li>
        <li><strong>The install tab opens as plain text.</strong> ScriptCat is not running or is disabled. Enable it and press the install link again.</li>
        <li><strong>An update never arrives.</strong> Confirm the script's <code>@updateURL</code> resolves — open it directly; it must return the raw JavaScript, not an HTML page.</li>
        <li><strong>Two scripts fight.</strong> Only one script in this collection owns a given capability (keys, toolbar, removal). Disable the older script rather than running both.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
